data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1197,"item_id":"msg_0728c5d930c188df016adb40bdf28481919f8dd65df37f36c7","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"target_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The original exercise asks for compact E⊆R^(d−1) and dim(E×I)=dim(E)+1 (problem.md:3). The frozen test target explicitly adds nonemptiness with user approval and includes n=0, I=[0,1], and the concatenated Euclidean metric (frozen-target.md:3-17). The spec’s parameters, H001/H002, and conclusion match that frozen target. But R001 does not establish the dimension equality: it relies on unsupported Hausdorff-content/dimension implications and leaves edge-case and metric details incomplete.\",\"locations\":[\"problem.md:3\",\"frozen-target.md:3-17\",\"spec.json:/full_target\",\"spec.json:/parameters\",\"spec.json:/hypotheses\",\"spec.json:/conclusion\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument\"]},\"definition_reviews\":{},\"source_reviews\":{\"M001\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The supplied full-signature evidence identifies a theorem, the pinned commit, and axioms [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] (signature-evidence.json:4-20). The official pinned source confirms the complete conditions: EMetricSpace, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace on X; s:Set X; d:NNReal; (d:ENNReal)<dimH s; conclusion μH[d] s=∞. The intended Euclidean application is compatible when the Borel structure and coercion are supplied. This source result does not establish the separate content implications in R001.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M001/0/sources/M001/signature\",\"signature-evidence.json:/M001/0/sources/M001/axioms\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:94-98\",\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean:105-118\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/0\"]},\"M002\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The supplied full-signature evidence includes the signature and axioms (signature-evidence.json:31-49). The official source confirms [Countable β], f:β→α→ENNReal, a measure μ on measurable α, and the hypothesis ∀i, AEMeasurable (f i) μ. The proposed application does not supply the restricted Lebesgue measure and indicator-valued ENNReal functions as complete definitions, or prove measurability of the restricted indicators and the integral calculation connecting the result to cover cost. The hypothesis-check sentence alone does not establish those steps.\",\"locations\":[\"signature-evidence.json:/M002/0/sources/M002/signature\",\"signature-evidence.json:/M002/0/sources/M002/axioms\",\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean:360-371\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/applications/1/hypothesis_checks/0\"]}},\"structure_review\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The graph has one target P with one producer R001, and the listed roots feed that inference; H roots match the spec. However, AND-closure cannot accept P because the sole inference has blocking mathematical gaps. No packet replay was performed or claimed.\",\"locations\":[\"nl0.json:/propositions\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/inputs\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/output\",\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument\"]},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/0/text\",\"premises\":\"H002 compactness and the assertion that for every q>D there are arbitrarily inexpensive positive-diameter covers with the required scale controls.\",\"conclusion\":\"dim_H(E×I)≤D+1.\",\"reason\":\"The Hausdorff measure/dimension cover characterization and the claimed cover choice are not established from declared inputs. The replacement of zero-diameter members is not fully justified, and q>D is not restricted to the NNReal exponents used for Hausdorff measure.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"premises\":\"M001 gives H^s(E)=∞ and M002 gives the integral of a countable ENNReal sum.\",\"conclusion\":\"c_s(E,δ)≤c_(s+1)(F,δ), hence dim_H(F)≥s+1.\",\"reason\":\"The proof does not establish the relation between infinite Hausdorff measure and scale content, or between the content inequality and infinite Hausdorff measure/dimension. The local c_s definition supplies no such theorem. The integration and application calculation is also incomplete.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/2/text\",\"premises\":\"H001 and projection F→I.\",\"conclusion\":\"dim_H(F)≥1 when D=0, and the claimed equality when n=0.\",\"reason\":\"Lipschitz dimension monotonicity, dim_H([0,1])=1, and the n=0 isometry/dimension conclusion are neither declared sources nor proved in the argument. The chosen x₀ is unused.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/locals\",\"premises\":\"F is locally defined as E×[0,1], while the target specifies the concatenated Euclidean metric.\",\"conclusion\":\"The cover-diameter and projection arguments apply to the target metric.\",\"reason\":\"The local definition does not state F’s metric or justify its correspondence to the target metric. The product diameter claim is not derived from the declared calculation policy, and the zero-diameter and n=0 cases remain incomplete.\"}]}","logprobs":[]}

